WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.701
Welcome back!

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.202
-What is up?!

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:07.474
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.909
I'm very happy.
-You're very happy.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.011
-Yes.
I want to be happy tonight.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.446
We flipped the damn House!
-There you go.

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:16.048
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on!

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.618
-Way to go.
It's a big deal.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.320
-It is a big deal.
-And the last time
you were here,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.156
we talked about this initiative
you started

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.323
called Glam up the Midterms.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:25.792
You took this very seriously,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.760
and you invested
a lot of personal time.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.296
-You're not gonna ask me
about a bowl of popcorn

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.463
that I'm holding?

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.066
-Why do you have
a bowl of popcorn?

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.167
-I brought it from
your dressing room because...

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:39.139
now that we flipped the House,
Maxine Waters is now head

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:42.342
of the House Financial --
What is that called?

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.810
-Yeah, the --
-The Financial Committee,

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.947
which means she can ask
for Donald Trump's taxes,

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.550
and I'm just gonna sit back
and watch.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.518
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.687
Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.856
That is pro--
I would guess that would be

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.358
Donald Trump's least --
That would be his last choice

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:00.493
for who would be in charge
of that committee.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.228
-Yeah.
He doesn't like her.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.931
-No.
-Because he's a racist.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.298
-Oh, yeah.
That's one of the reasons.

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:07.366
That's definitely
one of the reasons.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.068
-Oh, oh!
And a misogynist. Sorry.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.805
-Oh, yeah, that's right.
She ticks a lot of boxes.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.205
-Ticks a lot of boxes, yeah.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:15.174
No, I'm so excited.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.077
And I did start this
Glam up the Midterms campaign.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.547
I was out there
registering young voters,

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.914
trying to get them involved,

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:25.251
and I got so many messages
today on social media

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.687
all day long,
on Instagram, on Twitter,

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.488
all these young people
all over the country,

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.959
sending me photos of going to
vote for the first time,

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.861
going to vote in a midterm
for the first time

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.596
gathering with
groups of friends,

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.664
and I was really moved.

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.833
And I'm not the cause
of any of that.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.902
I just think
that they are responding

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.504
to things
they're seeing in our country

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.373
that they don't feel
are right and just and fair.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:50.576
And I want to thank all
the young people out there

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:54.347
who got involved
for the first time.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.048
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:59.318
And I think
they're gonna stay involved,

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:02.254
and I'm seeing a lot of sadness
tonight on social media

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:04.824
from young people
who really fell in love,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.892
rightfully so, with Beto.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:09.662
-And I love him, too,
but I want everyone to realize

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:13.432
that no Democrat has ever gotten
that close in Texas.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.468
-Yeah.
-It's Texas!

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.603
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:20.005
You know?
And Beto's not going anywhere.

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:22.441
And we had a really great night,
and I think, you know,

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.678
when Republicans win, they go
celebrating in the streets

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.848
like, racists start
throwing parades for themselves,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.617
and we're punishing ourselves.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.151
But we had a really great night,

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.786
so let's be happy
for five minutes.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:37.623
-There you go -- five minutes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:42.394
I mean, I do think one of the
sad things is, like you said,

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:45.598
a very charismatic candidate
like Beto O'Rourke

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.500
doesn't break through
against Ted Cruz.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.236
Do you think,
with what you saw from him --

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.904
and a lot of people
are talking about this now --

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.706
should he run for president
in two years?

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.107
Is he a national candidate?

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.476
-I think he is.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.845
I'm gonna leave it up to him
to decide, probably.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.346
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.381
But I love --
I want him to win everything.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.184
I want him to win
Best Supporting Actress.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.619
I mean, like, I love the man.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.654
-Who doesn't?
He's magical.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.823
You know, I think a lot of us
haven't felt that way

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.526
about a politician since Obama,

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.462
and I think
Beto's gonna be great.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.998
Give the man a second,
and I'll follow him

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.767
wherever he wants to go, and I
think a lot of us feel that way.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.203
But tonight, beyond Beto -- and
this is what I want to stress --

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.738
was a great night.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.441
We had a Native American
gay woman

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.177
flip a seat blue in Kansas.
-Kansas!

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.979
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.613
-In Kansas!

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.682
That's -- That's amazing.

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.518
Sharice Davids.
And she's awesome.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.219
It's the gayest thing
to happen in Kansas

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.488
since a house fell on the
Wicked Witch of the West.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.123
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.459
I mean -- Oh!
You guys don't know this maybe

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:50.296
'cause you've been here,
but voters in Michigan tonight

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.799
voted to legalize marijuana!

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:56.669
-That's fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.239
-And that's the only thing
I know about Michigan.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.739
[ Laughter ]
-You now have one fact.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:03.542
-I now have on fact.
But it's a good one.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.744
-You also --
You got to spend time

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:09.248
with former Vice President
Joe Biden in Las Vegas.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:13.686
-Yes, yes.
-How was your time with him?

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.488
-It was great.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.257
He didn't know who I was.
-Yeah.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.791
-But that was fine.
He shouldn't.

00:04:19.791 --> 00:04:21.761
He's Joe Biden.
And it was great.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.129
It's part of the
Glam up the Midterms campaign.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.764
We went all over.
We went to Phoenix,

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:27.400
we went to Vegas,
we went to Detroit,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.502
went to San Diego
before the California primaries.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:33.172
I went canvassing.
We did what we could.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.175
We went to Arizona.
I don't know yet if we know

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.910
what happened,
but Arizona has a great

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.945
Democratic candidate
running for Senate tonight,

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:42.114
Kyrsten Sinema,
and we're still waiting

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.783
to find out what happens,
but she would be the first

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:48.053
bisexual woman --
openly bisexual woman --

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:49.321
in Congress ever.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.056
And not only that,
but she would be

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.459
the first "Kirsten"
in the Senate

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.695
who spells her name with a Y.
-Okay.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.196
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.364
And, listen, think about
how much hope that would give

00:04:59.364 --> 00:05:02.668
all the horrible
Karens out there

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.205
who spell their name
K-A-R-Y-N.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.507
Or all the awful Ashleys

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:12.011
who spell their name
A-S-H-L-E-I-G-H.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.312
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:14.613
I mean, that's terrible.

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:16.315
-Yeah.
She would give them hope.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.551
-Give them some inspiration.
-Yeah.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.419
So I think it's pretty close
in Arizona right now

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.587
so hopefully she pulls through.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.722
-Did you vote today,
or did you vote early?

00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:25.758
-No, I voted early, yeah.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:29.996
I voted with an absentee ballot,
and then I sent it in.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:32.364
-And do you get a sticker
when you do that?

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.567
-I do get a sticker, yeah.
-Gotcha.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.069
-They give you a little sticker.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.271
-In the ballot
when they send it to you?

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:41.607
-No, Seth, that comes as
a special FedEx delivery.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.911
No, yeah.
It comes in the same envelope.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:48.080
-'Cause that seems expensive
if they would FedEx everybody.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.715
-People love
those stupid stickers.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.184
-They love their stickers.
-Social media was crazy today.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.419
-Yeah.
People were really happy.

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:56.889
-What about pizza to the polls?

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.957
Have you guys heard about this?
-No.

00:05:58.957 --> 00:06:01.060
-Yeah, no, this is real.
Pizza to the polls.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:04.063
All the people
waiting in line forever

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.799
because Republicans have made it
impossible to vote.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:09.668
So people waiting in line
for hours,

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.472
you can go to
PizzaToThePolls.com

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:15.174
or dot org or dot something,
and you can pay to have pizzas

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.242
delivered to the people
waiting in line.

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:21.347
I spent $100 to send pizza
to the polls.

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.549
Meanwhile, there are members
of my extended family

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.051
I haven't spoken to
in seven years.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.652
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:30.289
But there I am --
"Okay, pizza to the polls!

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.991
Pizza to the polls!"

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:34.394
-I'm sure they understand
and will forgive you.

